-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. mxdrfile, Copyright (c) 2014 Jon Kapla  --  BSD 3-Clause License
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Reading and writing of Gromacs .xtc and .trr trajectory files relies on the
mxdrfile package by Jon Kapla, http://kaplajon.github.io/mxdrfile/, which is
distributed under the BSD 3-Clause license. The full license text is retained
in the header of each of the following files:

    import_functions/import_xtc.m
    import_functions/import_trr.m
    custom_functions/decompose_traj.m
    custom_functions/extract_vxvy_from_trr.m
    custom_functions/extract_vz_from_trr.m

Redistribution of these files, in source or binary form, must retain that
copyright notice, the list of conditions and the accompanying disclaimer. The
name of the author may not be used to endorse or promote derived products
without specific prior written permission.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Other derived functions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following functions were adapted from or inspired by freely available
MATLAB code by other authors, who are credited in the headers of the respective
files. Where an original license applies, it governs that file:

    general_functions/show_arrow.m     adapted from mArrow3.m by Georg
                                       Stillfried, MATLAB File Exchange, 2009
    general_functions/show_atom.m      inspired by molecule3D.m by
                                       Andre Ludwig (aludwig@phys.ethz.ch)
    general_functions/show_atomo.m     Octave compatible version of the above

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Bundled reference data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The toolbox ships tabulated values taken from the scientific literature, such
as the revised Shannon ionic and crystal radii, bond valence parameters from
the IUCr, atomic scattering factors from Waasmaier & Kirfel (1995), and
published force field parameters for CLAYFF, INTERFACE, MINFF and others. The
original publications are cited next to the data in the corresponding files and
should be cited when the data is used.
